WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.578
"Hello!" Yog sang out, appearing suddenly in the middle of the sitting room.

2
00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:12.995
Zann spun around, startled. Over an hour had passed since he and his friends had been locked in the suite.

3
00:00:12.996 --> 00:00:16.384
Darb and the girls were playing with a deck of cards they'd found.

4
00:00:16.385 --> 00:00:19.125
But Zann was too restless to sit still.

5
00:00:19.126 --> 00:00:25.776
He was wandering from window to window, staring out at the palace courtyard while trying to figure out what to do.

6
00:00:25.777 --> 00:00:30.448
Jumping to her feet, Perda asked Yog,"Did you come to let us out?"

7
00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:34.555
Yog smiled. "Sorry, no. I'm here to conjure your dinner."

8
00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:37.273
"Where's Zing?" Zann demanded.

9
00:00:37.274 --> 00:00:41.714
"Who? Oh, the dragon," Yog said. "Don't worry, he's fine.

10
00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:47.040
Zing's having a great time hanging out with some cute female vapor bounders in the palace menagerie."

11
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:52.656
"You can't keep us here." Gliss frowned at him. "It's not right."

12
00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:57.601
Yog sighed. "Look, you have to understand it's not safe for you out there.

13
00:00:57.602 --> 00:01:01.898
Especially you two Reds. There are still trolls all over the city.

14
00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:05.104
You're better off staying here, under the protection of the palace."

15
00:01:05.105 --> 00:01:08.922
"The palace didn't protect the king and queen," Perda pointed out.

16
00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:14.299
Zann nodded. "We need to figure out what Morb is doing with all those Reds."

17
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.890
"We're working on that," Yog said. "We have spy flies everywhere."

18
00:01:18.891 --> 00:01:21.591
"So what have you found out?" Perda asked.

19
00:01:21.592 --> 00:01:25.009
Zann didn't expect Yog to answer. But he did.

20
00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:27.888
"Morb has changed his method," Yog said.

21
00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:32.367
"When he took the king and queen, he and his trolls zapped away with them immediately."

22
00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:37.010
Gliss looked sad. "Yeah, that's what happened with my parents."

23
00:01:37.011 --> 00:01:41.771
"The spy flies show that the trolls are still grabbing Reds," Yog went on.

24
00:01:41.772 --> 00:01:45.299
"But now they're holding them prisoner right here in First City."

25
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.101
"Really?" Darb said. "Where?"

26
00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:51.312
"The wild dragon pen at the zoo," Yog replied.

27
00:01:51.313 --> 00:01:54.487
"It's the only natural vacuum within the city limits.

28
00:01:54.488 --> 00:02:00.297
Dangerous dragon species are kept in that pen because dragons aren't able to use their magic in there."

29
00:02:00.298 --> 00:02:06.081
Gliss gasped. "The trolls are throwing the Reds in with a bunch of wild dragons?

30
00:02:06.082 --> 00:02:10.852
Even if the dragons can't use magic, the bigger ones could still kill someone!"

31
00:02:10.853 --> 00:02:17.198
"The dragons aren't there anymore." Yog paused, looking worried. "Nobody's sure what happened to them."

32
00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:23.816
"Why would Morb keep his prisoners in the city instead of zapping them away?" Zann wondered.

33
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:32.018
Yog shrugged. "Nobody knows. But Slib is supposed to be figuring out a plan to rescue the prisoners before Morb takes them away."

34
00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:34.570
Zann traded a glance with his friends.

35
00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.782
It sounded as if Yog didn't think much of Slib.

36
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:42.281
"Maybe we can help," Zann said. "If you let us out—"

37
00:02:42.282 --> 00:02:45.408
"Nice try." Yog gave him a sympathetic smile.

38
00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:48.952
"Now, what would you like for dinner?"

39
00:02:48.953 --> 00:02:54.605
Yog conjured plenty of food for them, along with pajamas and everything else they asked for.

40
00:02:54.606 --> 00:02:59.147
When Zann and his friends were busy eating, Yog stepped to the center of the room.

41
00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:03.081
"Good night," he said. "I'll be back in the morning to make you breakfast."

42
00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:09.156
Then he covered his mouth with his hand and whispered something. A second later he was gone.

43
00:03:09.157 --> 00:03:12.512
"Did anybody hear the password?" Zann asked.

44
00:03:12.513 --> 00:03:15.512
Darb shook his head. "I was too far away."

45
00:03:15.513 --> 00:03:20.640
"We all were," Gliss said. "We would've needed a Swelling spell to hear it."

46
00:03:20.641 --> 00:03:25.785
"Oh well," Perda said. "Maybe we could try to hear it when he comes back in the morning."

47
00:03:25.786 --> 00:03:29.262
"I wonder why Morb is keeping the prisoners at the zoo."

48
00:03:29.263 --> 00:03:31.032
Gliss took a sip of her drink.

49
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:34.188
"Why wouldn't he just zap them away like the others?"

50
00:03:34.189 --> 00:03:37.828
"Maybe he left the trolls in charge," Darb suggested.

51
00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:41.259
"Without extra magic they can't zap anyone anywhere."

52
00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:46.783
Zann hadn't thought of that. "Trolls can't do much magic, can they?" he said.

53
00:03:46.784 --> 00:03:51.009
Darb shook his head. "They can't even conjure up enough food for themselves.

54
00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:55.107
That's why they're always causing trouble, raiding villages near their territory.

55
00:03:55.108 --> 00:04:02.818
Morb must be providing extra magic so they can zap themselves long distances and do everything else they've been doing lately."

56
00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:05.620
"So why did he stop?" Gliss wondered.

57
00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:09.867
Perda shrugged. "Maybe kidnapping the king and queen weakened him."

58
00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:13.074
Zann was already losing interest in the conversation.

59
00:04:13.075 --> 00:04:16.642
He didn't want to sit around, talking about Morb's trolls.

60
00:04:16.643 --> 00:04:23.001
As far as Zann was concerned, they needed to find Boz's Magic Master friends as soon as possible.

61
00:04:23.002 --> 00:04:26.336
He pushed away his plate. "Who cares why?

62
00:04:26.337 --> 00:04:31.072
Let's get some sleep so we'll be ready to find a way out of here first thing tomorrow."

63
00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:36.224
"Okay," Perda said. "Come on, Gliss. We'll take the big bedroom.

64
00:04:36.225 --> 00:04:39.521
The boys can take the other one."

65
00:04:39.522 --> 00:04:46.182
It had been a long, exhausting day, and despite his worries, Zann fell asleep almost immediately.

66
00:04:46.183 --> 00:04:52.005
He wasn't sure how long he'd been asleep when he was startled awake by something brushing against his face.

67
00:04:52.006 --> 00:04:56.264
"Who's there?" he blurted out, wondering if he was still dreaming.

68
00:04:56.265 --> 00:05:01.038
There was no answer except a soft snore from the direction of Darb's bed.

69
00:05:01.039 --> 00:05:05.848
It was dark in the room, but something pale was fluttering around Zann's head.

70
00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:12.598
It was a message moth! Zann sat up quickly, holding out his hand. The moth landed on his finger.

71
00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:16.785
Zann climbed out of bed, hurried to the window, and pulled back the curtain.

72
00:05:16.786 --> 00:05:21.139
It was almost dawn, and there was just enough light for him to see.

73
00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:26.273
Zann peered at the moth's wings. To his surprise one of them was blank.

74
00:05:26.274 --> 00:05:29.462
Whoever had sent this moth hadn't signed it.

75
00:05:29.463 --> 00:05:34.803
"That's weird," Zann thought, quickly turning his gaze to the other wing.

76
00:05:34.804 --> 00:05:40.279
Just a few words were scrawled there, and Zann's eyes widened as he read them.

77
00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:47.284
The password is zipflower.

